'''Josuè Subirà''' ({{IPA|ca|dʒozuˈɛ subiˈra|lang}}; born 25 May 1985) is a Baliscan politician and activist. He has served as the leader of the [[W:Left-wing nationalism|left-wing nationalist]] platform [[Razón y Justicia]] since 2024, and has been a delegate representing the [[Port Nou (commune district)|Port Nou]] [[commune district]], since 2015. Subirà ran for [[Secretary General of Balisca|Secretary General]] in the [[2018 Baliscan premiership election|2018]], and [[2024 Baliscan premiership election|2024 elections]], but was defeated in the final round of voting both times.

